Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the PROJ module
==========================================

qore-proj-module ships native PROJ and the ProjGeos source/AOT module, plus
compiler metadata. The doc package contains both API references and example
tests. Debhelper generates matching native/AOT debug symbols. ProjGeos needs
the independently packaged GEOS module, declared as a build/runtime dependency.

Use an isolated native build environment with the packaged Qore runtime and
libqore-dev, then install debian/control's Build-Depends. Qualification targets
Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with the Qore 3.0 SDK. Other releases/architectures need
matching SDKs and native tests. Cross builds fail explicitly because Qore tools
run during compilation. Use distribution PROJ (>= 8.0), including proj-data;
no bundled library or build-time network download is needed. The module disables
PROJ network access; offline transformations use the installed coordinate database.

The runtime and libqore SONAME minimum versions come from the SDK used to
compile the module. dh_shlibdeps supplies the required native library versions.
The runtime is not Multi-Arch: same.

Build and metadata rules
------------------------

AOT is enabled, source-tree qmod symlinks are disabled and noopt selects AOT
optimization level zero. QCC_JOBS=1 fixes codegen partitioning independently
of CPU count and GNU make jobserver load; independent targets still compile
in parallel. Timezone and locale are fixed. Qore tools use only this build and
the packaged modules, including metadata extraction. Debian prefix maps also
cover AOT compiler output.

The stripping wrapper copied from Qore preserves appended dependency and
source-location metadata; its real-ELF tests run during builds. dwz skips the
runtime because it does not support all LLVM DWARF forms in AOT output.

Source preparation and qualification
------------------------------------

Use a fresh version for each changed upload. This snapshot precedes 1.1.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.1.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../proj-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-proj-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../proj-package-work/qore-proj-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../proj-package-work/qore-proj-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../proj-package-work
    cp -a debian "../proj-package-work/qore-proj-module-$version/"
    cd "../proj-package-work/qore-proj-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory and run dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc
unprivileged with networking disabled. -B builds runtime/debug only; -A builds
documentation. nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS suppresses HTML generation, and the
nodoc profile also omits the doc package. Do not use nocheck for the full
qualification build; subsequent profile/reproducibility builds may use it.

Run both upstream suites. Installed tests copy only test scripts into a
temporary directory, preload the installed AOT companion and use no source
checkout. They exercise projections, batch and inverse transforms, geodesic
helpers, geometry topology and error recovery. A fresh qcc executable checks
Munich WGS84-to-UTM coordinates and the inverse geometry transform.

Check Lintian, hardening, matching debug symbols, AOT trailers, installed
source parity, a runtime-only install without the SDK, docs/debug coinstallation,
dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and reproducibility across distinct paths/job counts.
Retain hashes, dependency inventories and logs. Testing-PPA publication is
separate from approval for a final general release.
